{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgarSA8JSAQ1Mz6E3qpvd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've proved `walkAcc_correct` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof uses induction on the tree, letting `acc` vary in each step (`generalizing acc`). That's needed because the recursive calls to `walkAcc` pass a different accumulator than the one they start with:\n\n```lean\ntheorem walkAcc_correct (t : Tree α) (acc : List α) : walkAcc t acc = inorder t ++ acc := by\n  induction t generalizing acc with\n  | empty => simp [walkAcc, inorder]\n  | node l x r ihl ihr => simp [walkAcc, inorder, ihl, ihr, List.append_assoc]\n```\n\n- **Empty tree:** both sides reduce to `acc`.\n- **Node:** applying the induction hypotheses for the right subtree and then the left one turns `walkAcc l (x :: walkAcc r acc)` into `inorder l ++ x :: (inorder r ++ acc)`. Regrouping the list appends (`List.append_assoc`) shows this equals `inorder (node l x r) ++ acc`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":8049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517},"output_tokens":383,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcc49252-c6a4-40d7-94ac-3924d272c4b3","uuid":"c1c4c59d-de4b-4465-b2b2-2a278fa0bc20","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:17:48.288Z","request_id":"req_011CgarS9uQaRKGwLGV32nqJ"}
